                      (    forth6809.asm):01821         ; ------------------------------------------------------------
                      (    forth6809.asm):01822         ; Return-stack test harness (glossary section 3.3). Unlike
                      (    forth6809.asm):01823         ; every other test group in this file, these words operate
                      (    forth6809.asm):01824         ; directly on the return stack (S) - the same stack holding
                      (    forth6809.asm):01825         ; real subroutine return addresses, including this very test
                      (    forth6809.asm):01826         ; subroutine's own. Every >R/2>R is balanced by a matching
                      (    forth6809.asm):01827         ; R>/2R> within the same test body, before this test's own
                      (    forth6809.asm):01828         ; RTS - leaving one unbalanced would corrupt the return address
                      (    forth6809.asm):01829         ; needed to get back to TSTRUNNER (or whatever called it).
                      (    forth6809.asm):01830         ; Traced each word's own PULS/PSHS juggling by hand first to
                      (    forth6809.asm):01831         ; confirm this: >R/R>/2>R/2R> all temporarily lift the caller's
                      (    forth6809.asm):01832         ; own return address off S, do the actual move, then restore it
                      (    forth6809.asm):01833         ; on top - so the moved value ends up correctly nested one level
                      (    forth6809.asm):01834         ; inside the current subroutine's own return-stack frame,
                      (    forth6809.asm):01835         ; retrievable by a later R>/2R> in the same body, and cleanly
                      (    forth6809.asm):01836         ; gone by the time this test's own RTS runs.
                      (    forth6809.asm):01837         ; ------------------------------------------------------------
                      (    forth6809.asm):01838         
                      (    forth6809.asm):01839         ; ------------------------------------------------------------
                      (    forth6809.asm):01840         ; TSTTOR - unit test for >R and R> together. Includes an
                      (    forth6809.asm):01841         ; intermediate check (right after >R, before R>) confirming the
                      (    forth6809.asm):01842         ; value genuinely left the data stack - a pure round-trip check
                      (    forth6809.asm):01843         ; could pass even if both words were broken no-ops, since the
                      (    forth6809.asm):01844         ; value would never actually have left.
                      (    forth6809.asm):01845         ; ------------------------------------------------------------
