F8E2                  (    forth6809.asm):14253         SUBSTITUTEW: ; REWRITE: was a plain substring search-and-replace on
                      (    forth6809.asm):14254                      ; the bare registered name (via SEARCHW), which found
                      (    forth6809.asm):14255                      ; "girl" and replaced only that span, leaving surrounding
                      (    forth6809.asm):14256                      ; "%...%" delimiters untouched in the output - and never
                      (    forth6809.asm):14257                      ; returned the substitution count ANS requires as a
                      (    forth6809.asm):14258                      ; third stack item. Per the ANS spec (forth-standard.org/
                      (    forth6809.asm):14259                      ; standard/string/SUBSTITUTE), SUBSTITUTE must scan for
                      (    forth6809.asm):14260                      ; text between '%' (ASCII $25) delimiter pairs
                      (    forth6809.asm):14261                      ; specifically: "%%" collapses to a single '%' (count
                      (    forth6809.asm):14262                      ; unchanged); a name matching the REPLACES registration
                      (    forth6809.asm):14263                      ; has the ENTIRE "%name%" span - delimiters included -
                      (    forth6809.asm):14264                      ; replaced by the substitution text (count incremented);
                      (    forth6809.asm):14265                      ; a non-matching name is passed through unchanged,
                      (    forth6809.asm):14266                      ; delimiters and all (count unchanged); an unpaired
                      (    forth6809.asm):14267                      ; trailing '%' with no closing delimiter passes the
                      (    forth6809.asm):14268                      ; residue through unchanged. Confirmed via MAME testing
                      (    forth6809.asm):14269                      ; against a real template. GLOBALS is fully packed
                      (    forth6809.asm):14270                      ; (256/256), so this reuses MSCR/MSCR2/MSCR3/MSCR4
                      (    forth6809.asm):14271                      ; (confirmed untouched by SUBCOPY) rather than adding
                      (    forth6809.asm):14272                      ; dedicated cells: MSCR = current read position, MSCR2 =
                      (    forth6809.asm):14273                      ; running substitution count, MSCR3/MSCR4 = local scratch
                      (    forth6809.asm):14274                      ; per %-pair found. Reuses the existing COMPAREW for name
                      (    forth6809.asm):14275                      ; matching rather than a new comparison loop.
